From e5da34177368960c9707df6c7b8d55e6c4ab081a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:29:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: penalize the dispel reserve once, not twice

The mana-needed-for-final-teleport penalty in
borg_attack_aux_spell_dispel() was applied twice: once with the class's
reserve and once more with a fixed six - a subset of the first for
every class, since every class reserve is six or more.  The penalty
doubled for every class, most visibly for the Mage whose reserve is
exactly six.  Keep the class-based block.

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c b/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
index 45c5d140a..d09c14469 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
@@ -2708,11 +2708,6 @@ static int borg_attack_aux_spell_dispel(
         && (borg.trait[BI_CURSP] - spell_power < penalty))
         b_n = b_n - (spell_power * 750);
 
-    /* Really penalize use of mana needed for final teleport */
-    /* (6 pts for mage) */
-    if ((borg.trait[BI_MAXSP] > 30) && (borg.trait[BI_CURSP] - spell_power) < 6)
-        b_n = b_n - (spell_power * 750);
-
     /* never tap if we previously missed a tap */
     if (target_closest < 0 && BORG_ATTACK_TAP_UNLIFE == typ && b_n > 0) {
         target_closest = 0;
